WEBVTT

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.330
Imam Ibn al-Qayyim once said:

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:07.740
<i>Faqira’atu ayatin
bi-tafakkurin wa tafahhumin</i>

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:12.250
<i>khayrun min qira’ati khatmatin
bi-ghayri tadabburin wa tafahhumin,</i>

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:18.008
<i>wa anfa‘u lil-qalbi, wa ad‘a ila
husuli al-‘arabiyyati wa ma‘aniha.</i>

00:00:18.008 --> 00:00:21.385
Reciting a single verse
with reflection and understanding

00:00:21.385 --> 00:00:24.909
is better than reciting an entire
completion of the Qur’an

00:00:24.909 --> 00:00:27.646
without contemplation or comprehension.

00:00:27.646 --> 00:00:29.585
It is more beneficial for the heart

00:00:29.585 --> 00:00:32.578
and more conducive to acquiring
proficiency in Arabic

00:00:32.578 --> 00:00:34.377
and understanding its meanings.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:38.066
For years, we relied on translations,

00:00:38.066 --> 00:00:40.925
feeling a thick veil
between us and the Divine.

00:00:40.925 --> 00:00:43.546
But after learning Arabic
through Sabeel Institute,

00:00:43.546 --> 00:00:45.226
that veil was lifted.

00:00:45.226 --> 00:00:49.978
We’ve grown from basic learners to true
talib al-ilm, students of knowledge.

00:00:49.978 --> 00:00:52.631
Through the volumes
of the Madinah Arabic series,

00:00:52.631 --> 00:00:55.450
from simple nouns
to advanced sentence structures,

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.400
we mastered nahw and sarf,

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.495
so we can now read classical texts
without harakat,

00:01:00.495 --> 00:01:03.770
taking apart every word,
state, and root letter.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:06.670
By grouping vocabulary
like three-letter roots,

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:08.990
like unlocking kaf, ta, ba,

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:12.644
to discover kataba,
katibun, and maktabun,

00:01:12.644 --> 00:01:15.264
our comprehension grew exponentially.

00:01:15.264 --> 00:01:17.236
And through group study sessions,

00:01:17.236 --> 00:01:20.146
every complex, conditional,
and irregular verb

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.085
became permanently engraved.

00:01:23.152 --> 00:01:26.495
We embraced our learning mistakes
as sacred stepping stones.

00:01:26.495 --> 00:01:29.586
Our beloved teachers hold our hands
throughout the program,

00:01:29.586 --> 00:01:34.243
and their clarity makes these golden texts
breathe with grammatical emphasis.

00:01:34.243 --> 00:01:36.024
With this understanding of Arabic,

00:01:36.024 --> 00:01:37.749
we are now the inheritors.

00:01:37.749 --> 00:01:40.050
As Umar ibn al-Khattab said:

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:43.520
<i>Ta‘allamu al-‘arabiyyata
fa-innaha tathbitu al-‘aqla</i>

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.347
<i>wa tazidu fi al-maru’ah.</i>

00:01:45.347 --> 00:01:47.074
Arabic is part of our deen.

00:01:47.074 --> 00:01:50.034
It sharpens the intellect
and elevates virtue.

00:01:50.034 --> 00:01:53.688
But our transformation
wasn’t just academic, it was spiritual.

00:01:53.688 --> 00:01:56.109
We don’t need approximate
translations anymore;

00:01:56.109 --> 00:01:58.797
we now stand directly before the ayat.

00:01:58.797 --> 00:02:01.646
We experience the i‘jaz,
the living miracle,

00:02:01.646 --> 00:02:04.520
recognizing the specific power
of Allah’s words.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:08.720
Madinah Arabic classes at Sabeel Institute
teach classical Arabic

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:13.655
using examples straight from the Qur’an,
hadith, and Islamic tradition.

00:02:13.655 --> 00:02:15.230
We can take ayat, such as

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:20.352
<i>Inna anzalnahu Qur’anan ‘arabiyyan
la‘allakum ta‘qilun.</i>

00:02:20.352 --> 00:02:23.122
Indeed, We have sent it down
as an Arabic Qur’an

00:02:23.122 --> 00:02:24.753
so that you may understand.

00:02:24.753 --> 00:02:28.788
And now, we can grasp the core essence
of spiritual terminology.

00:02:28.788 --> 00:02:32.287
This curriculum turned academic
into active worship.

00:02:32.287 --> 00:02:34.355
We are no longer merely students;

00:02:34.355 --> 00:02:37.078
we are humble carriers
of a sacred tradition,

00:02:37.078 --> 00:02:41.293
eternally grateful that the Qur’an
now speaks directly to our hearts.

00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:44.922
If you think that your salah
is a mechanical, robotic routine,

00:02:44.922 --> 00:02:47.243
if you are looking for a transformation,

00:02:47.243 --> 00:02:49.923
if you are craving
a deeper connection with Allah,

00:02:49.923 --> 00:02:51.863
drenched in profound khushu,

00:02:51.863 --> 00:02:55.017
then join our next cohort
at Sabeel Institute.
